  sender: "C.N.A. \u2014 O.T.U."
  subject: "Watcher (C-Watcher034-CR)"
  body: "<b>C.N.A. \u2014 ANOMALY FIELD RECORD</b>\nCONTROLLED DOCUMENT \u2014 INTERNAL USE ONLY\n\n<b>DEPARTMENT:</b> Observation and Telemetry Unit (O.T.U.)\n<b>DOCUMENT TYPE:</b> Anomaly Identification & Response Record\n<b>DESIGNATION:</b> C-Watcher034-CR\n<b>REGISTERED NAME:</b> WATCHER\n<b>THREAT LEVEL:</b> 4-CRITICAL\n<b>BEHAVIOR CLASS:</b> AGGRESSIVE\n<b>RESPONSE AUTHORITY:</b> O.T.U. \u2014 Observation and Telemetry Unit\n<b>O.T.U. INTERVENTION:</b> AUTHORIZED \u2014 SILENCE PROTOCOL\n<b>C.R.U. DEPLOYMENT:</b> NOT REQUIRED UNDER STANDARD CONDITIONS\n<b>RECORD STATUS:</b> ACTIVE\n\n<b>01. GENERAL DESCRIPTION</b>\nWatcher is a hostile humanoid anomaly primarily observed through active surveillance systems.\nThe entity possesses a tall, narrow body, unusually elongated upper limbs, and two large, round eyes located on its face.\nWatcher shares a significant physical resemblance with another registered anomaly known as Demon. The primary distinguishing characteristic between the two entities is the presence of visible eyes.\nDespite its name and appearance, Watcher\u2019s primary threat mechanism is auditory rather than visual.\nUpon detecting an active surveillance camera, the entity will rapidly approach the device and remain directly in front of its lens.\nDuring this period, Watcher appears capable of detecting sounds transmitted through the observation system.\nThe anomaly presents a significant threat to personnel assigned to surveillance duties.\nUnlike other hostile entities, Watcher does not require physical intervention. Personnel can survive an encounter by maintaining complete silence until the entity withdraws.\n\n<b>02. PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTICS</b>\nWatcher possesses several identifiable physical features:\n\u2022 A tall, narrow humanoid structure.\n\u2022 Exceptionally long upper limbs.\n\u2022 A body silhouette closely resembling that of Demon.\n\u2022 Two large, round eyes positioned on its face.\n\u2022 A narrow torso with proportions inconsistent with normal human anatomy.\nThe presence of two visible eyes is the anomaly\u2019s most reliable identifying characteristic.\nUnder low-light conditions, the entity may be difficult to distinguish from Demon due to their nearly identical body structures.\nPersonnel are advised to prioritize examination of the facial region when identifying either entity.\nThe function of Watcher\u2019s unusually large eyes remains undetermined.\nAlthough the entity appears capable of detecting surveillance equipment, its primary method of locating observation personnel is believed to involve auditory detection.\n\n<b>03. OBSERVED BEHAVIOR</b>\nWatcher exhibits deliberate and hostile behavior toward active surveillance equipment.\nThe anomaly may initially appear stationary within a monitored area.\nOnce it detects a camera, Watcher will immediately advance toward the device at an unusually high speed.\nUpon reaching the camera, the entity will position itself directly in front of the lens and remain stationary.\nDuring this period, Watcher appears to monitor audio transmitted through the observation system.\nThe anomaly is capable of detecting sounds originating from the operator\u2019s microphone.\nPotential sources of detection include:\n\u2022 Spoken communication.\n\u2022 Coughing or other involuntary vocal sounds.\n\u2022 Sudden noises near the microphone.\n\u2022 Background sounds captured by the active audio input.\nIf an audible signal is detected, Watcher may immediately identify the location of observation personnel.\nIf no sound is detected, the entity will eventually withdraw from the camera.\nThe duration of this listening period has not been established.\nWatcher does not appear to require direct visual contact with personnel to locate them.\n\n<b>04. THREAT ASSESSMENT</b>\nWatcher is classified as a hostile anomaly due to its ability to locate observation personnel through transmitted audio and its potentially fatal response to detected sound.\nThe primary danger is not the entity\u2019s initial approach toward surveillance equipment.\nIt is the possibility of an audible signal being transmitted from the observation station.\nEven a brief sound may be sufficient for Watcher to identify the operator\u2019s location.\nPersonnel who attract its attention are not recovered.\nThe exact method by which the entity reaches or eliminates personnel remains undetermined.\nA significant operational risk is the physical similarity between Watcher and Demon.\nThese anomalies require opposing response procedures.\nWatcher requires silence, while Demon must be repelled through high-volume audio.\nIncorrect identification may result in personnel attempting a response that directly increases the threat.\n\n<b>05. DETECTION PROCEDURE</b>\nWatcher is most reliably identified through visual inspection of surveillance feeds.\nO.T.U. personnel must inspect the facial characteristics of any humanoid anomaly approaching an active surveillance camera.\nUpon detecting a suspected manifestation:\n1. Maintain observation of the affected camera channel.\n2. Examine the entity\u2019s body structure and facial features.\n3. Look for two large, round eyes.\n4. Compare the observed characteristics with the Field Manual.\n5. Confirm the entity\u2019s identity before initiating the appropriate response procedure.\nThe presence of eyes is the primary distinguishing characteristic between Watcher and Demon.\nPersonnel must not rely exclusively on body shape or movement patterns.\nIf the entity has two visible eyes, initiate the Watcher silence protocol.\nDo not attempt verbal communication while identification is in progress.\nAn incorrect classification may result in a fatal response error.\n\n<b>06. RESPONSE PROCEDURE</b>\nWatcher responds to sounds transmitted through the observation system.\nThe authorized O.T.U. response is complete silence.\nNo physical intervention or specialized equipment is required under standard encounter conditions.\nUpon positive identification:\n1. Immediately cease all verbal communication.\n2. Do not transmit reports through the radio.\n3. Avoid producing sounds near the active microphone.\n4. Remain silent while Watcher occupies the camera.\n5. Continue observing the entity without audible interaction.\n6. Wait until Watcher withdraws from the camera.\n7. Verify that the affected camera feed has returned to its normal condition.\nDo not attempt to repel Watcher using loud sounds.\nDo not contact the C.R.U. while the entity remains in its listening state.\nDo not assume the entity has departed simply because no movement is observed.\nWatcher may remain stationary while actively monitoring the observation system.\nThe entity\u2019s withdrawal must be visually confirmed before normal communication resumes.\n\n<b>07. FAILURE CONDITIONS</b>\nFailure to maintain silence during an active Watcher encounter may result in immediate personnel loss.\nThe following conditions significantly increase operational risk:\n\u2022 Mistaking Watcher for Demon.\n\u2022 Speaking after the entity reaches the camera.\n\u2022 Attempting to communicate through the radio.\n\u2022 Producing unintended sounds near the microphone.\n\u2022 Assuming low-volume speech cannot be detected.\n\u2022 Attempting to repel the entity through loud audio.\n\u2022 Resuming communication before the entity withdraws.\n\u2022 Failing to verify that the affected camera is clear.\nThe absence of movement must not be interpreted as successful resolution of the encounter.\nA stationary Watcher may still be listening.\nOnce an audible signal has been detected, the opportunity for corrective action may no longer exist.\n\n<b>08. POST-ENCOUNTER PROCEDURE</b>\nFollowing Watcher\u2019s withdrawal, O.T.U. personnel must verify that the affected camera remains operational.\nNormal surveillance activities may resume once the immediate threat has passed.\nAny required incident report must be transmitted only after the entity has completely withdrawn.\nThe disappearance of Watcher does not indicate permanent removal.\nSubsequent manifestations remain possible during the same observation shift.\nPersonnel must continue monitoring all assigned camera channels and remain prepared to repeat the silence protocol.\nC.R.U. deployment is not required following a successfully resolved standard encounter unless otherwise directed by supervisory personnel.\n\n<b>09. O.T.U. PERSONNEL DIRECTIVE</b>\nWatcher must be positively identified before any response is initiated.\n<b>VERIFY THE PRESENCE OF TWO LARGE EYES.</b>\n<b>DO NOT CONFUSE WATCHER WITH DEMON.</b>\n<b>DO NOT SPEAK WHILE THE ENTITY IS LISTENING.</b>\n<b>DO NOT USE THE RADIO.</b>\n<b>AVOID ALL AUDIBLE NOISE NEAR THE MICROPHONE.</b>\n<b>REMAIN SILENT UNTIL THE ENTITY HAS COMPLETELY WITHDRAWN.</b>\n\n<b>C.N.A. \u2014 OBSERVATION AND TELEMETRY UNIT</b>\nOBSERVE. IDENTIFY. NEUTRALIZE.\n<i>An empty room is not necessarily a clear room.</i>"
